  "comment": "Order defines the 12-bit GPU material ID; id 0 is always air (implicit). class: solid|powder|liquid|gas. density drives displacement (air=10). emission: 0-255 glow. moveEvery: viscosity (move only every Nth tick). wanders: critter scuttle. opaque: liquid renders as a surface, not translucent media. colors: 3 palette variants picked by the voxel state nibble. Tags feed reactions.json (tag:xxx matchers). Worldgen (worldgen.wgsl + world.cpp) and world.h assume the ID order of everything listed here \u2014 append new materials at the end, never reorder. hardness: 0-255 blast/dig resistance (class defaults: solid 60, powder 12, liquid 4, gas 0; 255 on sources/void = practically indestructible). molten: what the laser/heat melt brush (mode 2) converts this material into; absent = vaporized to air; 255-hardness matter is immune.",
