    {
      "comment": "Blood. The `stain` block is what marks what it touches: at 90 per-mille a splash grabs the surfaces around it within a second or so, and `consume` 6 means roughly one stained voxel in 160 is eaten away per stain event, so blood slowly pits what it soaks without ever running away with itself (CLAUDE.md rule 2 — see DESIGN.md §6). The renderer picks blood's viscous shading (no ripple bands, a wet sheen, a smooth field normal so it does not read as gelatin cubes) off the authored moveEvery + opacity pair, not off a material ID — see isViscousLiquid in common.wgsl.",
